UID:10083306-1790438400-1790447400@thedirt.online
SUMMARY:Film: The Palestine Exception
DESCRIPTION:You are invited to a special screening and discussion as part of the Davis Palestine Film Series. We will be showing the documentary “The Palestine Exception\,” followed by a panel and conversation. \nAbout the Film:\nDescribed as a “searing and unflinchingly honest account of what it means to stand for something\,” this documentary explores the immense consequences of speaking up against injustice. It offers a vital look at how institutional power attempts to enforce silence on its critics\, a theme that feels particularly urgent for our present moment. \nEvent Details:\nDate: Saturday\, September 26\nTime: 4:00 PM – 6:30 PM (please give yourself extra time to travel and park your car or bike; programming will begin promptly at 4:00)\nLocation: UC Davis Cruess Hall Theater\nAddress: 375 California Ave\, Davis\nParking: Easy & FREE parking available on-site on campus\, just across from Cruess Hall
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/film-the-palestine-exception/
LOCATION:Cruess Hall\, UC Davis
CATEGORIES:Community
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://thedirt.online/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/davis-palestine-series-flyer.png
END:VEVENT
